These estimates are consistent with the non-detection of CGWs by the directed searches towards the galactic centre using LIGO-Virgo data from the third observing run (Abbott et al., 2022). Using the spatial and frequency distribution models that we employed to study the detectability of lensed signals, we estimate the detection probability of (all) CGWs to be \\sim 0-2\\% with \\epsilon=10^{-7} and coherent integration time of 1 yr7. For the coherent integration times of a few hrs employed in Abbott et al. (2022), the expected detection probability is almost zero.

